erefore, the 2 is the highest remaining card and is absolutely unbeatable. Playing the 2 guarantees I win the trick and retain the lead (control).\n3. **Play Single 9**: Breaking the pair is inefficient and risky, as opponents can easily beat a single 9.\n\nReason: Playing the **Single ♦2** is the winning move. Since there are no bombs or jokers left, the 2 acts as the "Boss Card" and guarantees the initiative. After the 2 clears the board, I will be left with a pair of 9s. Since it will be my turn again, I can play the pair of 9s immediately to empty my hand and win the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦2"]}'}
